{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.WedderburnIdempotents","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WedderburnIdempotents","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Idempotents","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.SimpleModule.WedderburnArtin","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WedderburnIdempotents.exists_central_completeOrthogonalIdempotents","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WedderburnIdempotents.exists_central_completeOrthogonalIdempotents","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WedderburnIdempotents.lean#L33-L58","doc":"**From an Artin–Wedderburn equivalence to the central idempotent system.**\n\nAn algebra equivalence `A ≃ₐ M₁ × ⋯ × M_N` — which\n`IsSemisimpleRing.exists_algEquiv_pi_matrix_divisionRing_finite` supplies for\nany finite-dimensional semisimple algebra — transports the standard idempotents\nof the product back to `A`. The result is exactly the data\n`QOU.Hecke.WedderburnDecomp` asks for: **idempotent, pairwise orthogonal,\ncentral, summing to `1`**.\n\nThe first three of those four come straight from Mathlib\n(`CompleteOrthogonalIdempotents.single`, transported by `.map`); centrality is\nsupplied here.\n\n**What this does not give**, and it is the whole remaining gap:\n`WedderburnDecomp` indexes its idempotents by `Partition n`, while\nArtin–Wedderburn produces an index of unconstrained size. Matching the two —\nthat the blocks of `H_n(q)` are indexed by the partitions of `n`, and there are\nno others — is Mathas (1999) §3.43, which is not in Mathlib and not in this\ntree. So this closes the *construction* of the idempotents and leaves the\n*indexing* open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WedderburnIdempotents.central_of_equiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WedderburnIdempotents.central_of_equiv","kind":"theorem","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WedderburnIdempotents.lean#L25-L31","doc":"**Centrality transports along a ring equivalence.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.WedderburnIdempotents.single_one_central","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.WedderburnIdempotents.single_one_central","kind":"theorem","line":12,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/WedderburnIdempotents.lean#L12-L22","doc":"**In a finite product of rings, `Pi.single i 1` is central.**\n\nMathlib's `CompleteOrthogonalIdempotents.single` gives idempotence, pairwise\northogonality and completeness of this family; centrality is the part it does\nnot carry, and the part `QOU.Hecke.WedderburnDecomp.central` asks for. ","signatureChunk":0}]}